```uvl
// Smart Home Automation System

// Rule for "Movie Mode" scene:
rule MovieModeScene {
    when 
        // Trigger: Scene initiated by user
        HomeScene == "Movie Mode"
        
        // Optional condition: No other scenes active
        Not(ActiveScenes.contains("Morning"))
    
    then
        // Action: Set lights to 10%
        Light.set(10)
}

// Safety constraint for "Smart Oven":
rule SmartOvenSafety {
    when
        // Trigger: User initiates oven operation
        Ovens > 0
        
        // Optional condition: Home status is not away
        HomeStatus!= "Away"

    then
        // Disable oven action
        Oven.disable()
}

// Dynamic disabling of "Air Conditioner" if window sensors report open:
rule AirConditionerDynamicDisable {
    when
        // Trigger: Any window sensor reports open
        WindowSensors.any()

        // Optional condition: All windows closed within 5 minutes
        All(Windows.closedIn(5))

    then
        // Dynamically disable air conditioner
        AirConditioner.disable()
}
```

This code translates the provided requirements into a structured format suitable for an event-driven system like those found in smart home automation systems. Each rule includes triggers, conditions, and actions necessary to achieve the desired functionality while adhering to the specified safety constraints.